    "notes": "Mapped terminal and roof parts, 24 rail alignments and five court footprints locate the station. The native terrain mask opens the covered platform volume below Jardin Atlantique. All road inputs and independent buildings remain unchanged. Three entrance bays and 24 sampled track passages remain open. The roof underside hides the planting from below. Standard PMTiles controls the mapped exteriors, roof court footprints and 24 rail alignments. The heights of the entrance, train floor and park deck are reconstructed from the photographs and standard viewer terrain. The model includes the main public entrance volume and the covered track passages. Shop interiors, transit operations, planting schedules and restricted station interiors are outside this model. The garden and forecourt follow the photographed configuration. The separate Tour Montparnasse remains a neighboring landmark."
  },
